  Preserve uniqueness when deriving channel IDs.

  Lowercasing, character replacement, and truncation can map distinct run
  IDs to the same channel—for example, IDs differing only by case or after
  the first 58 normalized characters. This can merge unrelated run traffic.

  Include a hash of the original ID whenever normalization changes or
  truncates it, or append a short hash unconditionally.


